    "selected_scope": "Selected exact original Theorem1.1, with its complete authored Lemma5.1/Theorem5.2 construction and the entire new local overlap, bounded-graph, cone-comparison and scaled-filling core. A finitely generated non-trivial group acts on a bounded-valence hyperbolic graph freely on its vertex set and every amenable quotient is trivial. No standalone small-cancellation proposition or torsion parameter variant is selected.",
    "difficulty_level": "H3",
    "difficulty_reason": "The authors must preserve a uniformly proper bounded-geometry hyperbolic action under the particular high-power fillings, using their complete cylinder-overlap and cone-metric comparison constructions. They then build noncommensurable elements that are conjugate in every finite quotient through an explicit characteristic-core argument inside the Rips kernel. The distinct-prime quotient and property(T) closing uses that new geometric and finite-quotient mechanism to kill all amenable quotients while retaining a non-trivial action; the packet includes the full authored obligations rather than only citing the small-cancellation foundation.",
    "literal_source_disclosure": "Original Proposition4.4(1) literally prints the denominator <g_i>, while the full filling family uses <u g_i^(n_i) u^(-1)> and Theorem4.3(2) prints Stab(Y)/H. Its entire proof closing and the original5.2 exact prime-order use are retained. The filling-family display also literally writes uY_g, and the source constant-list wording has delta_0 delta_1 without a separating comma. These original literals are preserved; no denominator, index or proof correction is supplied. Proposition4.4 is not independently selected as a corpus unit.",
    "source_page_boundary_receipt_sha256": "e635338a7882214771b42f13688363d8b29e8e097328354a90878fb1e07cc68a",
